COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff in
            collaboration with Sujatha Mohan. The reference sequence was
            derived from AC006483.3.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes one of six different actin proteins.
            Actins are highly conserved proteins that are involved in cell
            motility, structure, integrity, and intercellular signaling. The
            encoded protein is a major constituent of the contractile apparatus
            and one of the two nonmuscle cytoskeletal actins that are
            ubiquitously expressed. Mutations in this gene cause
            Baraitser-Winter syndrome 1, which is characterized by intellectual
            disability with a distinctive facial appearance in human patients.
            Numerous pseudogenes of this gene have been identified throughout
            the human genome. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2017].
